Blocker (full-suite gate): the implementation is complete (8 per-game presets, `docs/dev/game-configuration.md`, README/DEVELOPER/multi-repo/plugin doc updates, per-game preset unit guards). `GAMES_CONFIG=main-street npm run build` succeeds and the affected unit tests pass. The pre-commit full-suite gate cannot complete because the host is CPU-saturated by concurrent agent test runs (load average rose 25 → 82 on 16 cores, 30 Vitest processes), causing known contention timeouts in unrelated heavy tests:
- `tests/electron/vite-base-gating.test.ts` — two full Vite builds, timed out at 90s (already the configured budget);
- `tests/main-street/competitive-monte-carlo.test.ts` — 200-seed batch, timed out at 15s;
- `[vitest-worker]: Timeout calling "onTaskUpdate"` at teardown.

These are the same class as in-progress test-failure item CG-0MUIMM28K001W88F (`<suite exited 1>: npm --silent test`) and completed CG-0MS9M5UJP005PWD3 (Vitest worker RPC timeout under CPU contention). The failure set varies between runs (tap-reporter timeouts earlier; vite-base-gating/monte-carlo now), confirming it is environmental, not caused by this docs/config change. The one test-collection bug actually found and fixed here was the nested-Vitest timeout in `tests/tooling/vitest-tap-reporter.test.ts` (triage child CG-0MUILHPFY0070EKT).

Next action: wait for host load to fall, then run the full suite to populate the green full-suite cache and complete `implement.py finish`. If load does not clear, the full-suite gate must be re-run when the contention flake (CG-0MUIMM28K001W88F) lands.
